in this video i'm going to show you  exactly what apps and programs i  personally use as a west australian  architect  on the brand new  m1 ultra mac studio number one is  magnets magnets should be a default  feature on apple systems but  unfortunately it is not it is basically  an app that is replicating what windows  has done for years all it does is  literally snap your programs and your  windows to one side or another where you  see fit for your workflow i really got  sick of moving all the screens and apps  around without being able to just snap  them to corners split the screens in  half like you can do on the ipad so i  downloaded this app it cost a little bit  of money but it was worth every cent now  i'm sure apple is definitely going to  come out with this feature someday soon  but for the time being this is an  exceptional app number two is notion if  you haven't used notion before you're  missing out notion is a phenomenal app  that basically allows you to curate your  life now i can't exactly show you what's  on my notion because it is all private  client information so i'm going to show  a blurred out version as much as i can  but basically it holds all of my project  notes it holds all of my projects and  whenever i need to refresh my memory on  a project this is exactly where i go now  if you stay tuned to the end of this  video i'm going to show you a full  breakdown of every app on the system the  third one on the list is very obvious  and everybody should have some shape or  form of this program  for me it's onedrive onedrive allows me  to connect all of my projects across all  of my devices so if you aren't on some  sort of cloud system what are you doing  number four is team gantt and teamgantt  is basically a gantt chart that allows  you to schedule and program your work  for me personally we have a very large  team it requires a lot of finesse to be  able to manipulate and manage all of  those projects at once so the team gantt  chart allows a visual representation of  who's doing what when they're doing what  and when clients can expect their work  so if somebody rings up and goes hey  david where's my project where's it at i  can quickly look on this team gantt  chart and go no worries mate it's  exactly due on this date last but not  least is number five and that is pro  workflow there are a number of these  apps out there but for me personally  this one was the winner for architecture  simply put pro workflow is a time  management system all we use it for is  documenting time sheets and managing our  projects from a financial point of view  so you can check every single project  how it's going if it's doing well if  it's profitable if it's not  and how long a staff member or anybody  has spent individually on that project  specifically on that task and what  they've done in that time frame so when  a client asks hey david what did you do  for a hundred hours on this project all  you do is print out a spreadsheet from  pro workflow go here you go this is  exactly who worked on it when they  worked on it how long they worked on it  and what they did it makes all of those  hard conversations significantly easier  now just because i'm a nice guy i'm  going to show you exactly what's on the  m1 ultra all i ask in return is you  smash the like button down below for the  youtube algorithm so here's a quick  breakdown of what's on my dock running  through them one by one we have finder  safari to-do list outlook notion teams  calendar notes archicad 25 obviously  twin motion teamgantt and pro workflow  up the top we have onedrive creative  cloud which i have photoshop lightroom  and premiere pro installed and also  magnets that's it for me my name is  david thomich i'll see you next time
 

